<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mbabane</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mbabane is the capital and one of the largest cities of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eswatini">Eswatini</a>, in the highveld of the north-west. It grew from a trading post near the royal residence of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mbandzeni">Mbandzeni</a> and was chosen in 1902 as the administrative centre of the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> of Swaziland. It remains the seat of government, while the royal and legislative capital is at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lobamba">Lobamba</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mbabane.jpg" alt="Mbabane" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Athena Lao from Bulgaria · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mbabane_(6035476964).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
